  "notes": "The Enterprise Campus 48S spec table prints no PoE row: Port Layout \"1 GbE RJ45 1 (1G/100M/10M), 2.5 GbE RJ45 32 (2.5G/1G/100M/10M), 10 GbE RJ45 16 (10G/5G/2.5G/1G/100M/10M), 25G SFP28 4 (25G/10G/1G), 100G QSFP28 2 (100G), Console 1\", Max. Power Consumption 250W, Power Supply \"(2) Hot-swappable AC/DC 550W power modules\" - no per-port wattage, no budget. The PoE member of the Campus family is a separate model (ecs-48s-poe.json) with its own budget, so the absence is the product decision. Without `poeIn: false` all 49 copper sockets (the 1G row is the OOB management port, still copper) each asked for 12.95 W - **634.6 W**; this was the largest single inferred draw in the catalogue after the Gen1 48-port."
